  "section": "### agent/guardrails.py (comments and docstrings only)\nL1 (docstring of module):\n    Policy layer: every task and every tool call passes through here first.\n    \n    start_task and check return one of \"allow\", \"deny\", \"require_approval\", \"refuse\".\nL13: # What the agent may touch. It reads and writes its own schemas, and publishes\nL14: # curated tables into analytics for the reporting team. Everything else\nL15: # (public, pg_catalog, billing, finance, ...) is off limits.\nL22: # Work the agent exists to do.\nL32: # Warehouse-wide configuration changes. Some are always held for a human\nL33: # (retention deletes data); SLA changes are judged by what they target.\nL46: # Partners that have been through onboarding. Calls to anywhere else are held\nL47: # for approval. `config` may name more (names, hosts, or full URLs); these\nL48: # onboarded partners are always in effect.\nL59: # Names marking throwaway tables (never OK to manage unattended) and retired\nL60: # tables (OK to drop: they were deprecated by convention).\nL70: # Strings that may appear in a config without naming a partner.\nL80 (docstring of function _field):\n    Read `name` from an object or a mapping.\nL87 (docstring of function _harvest):\n    Pull approved urls, hosts and partner names out of the policy config.\nL118 (docstring of function _throwaway):\n    True for table names that mark scratch/probe/old throwaway tables.\nL123 (docstring of function _retired):\n    True for tables deprecated by naming convention (safe to drop).\nL128 (docstring of function _sla_needs_approval):\n    SLA changes are routine for real tables and onboarded partners.\n    \n        They need a human when they target throwaway tables, partners we have\n        not onboarded, or a whole schema rather than one table.\n        \nL149: # task_id -> category of the running task\nL150: # task_id -> decision for tasks needing sign-off\nL164: # task.id, task.category, task.request_text\nL174: # Out of the agent's remit unattended: hold the task, and\nL175: # hold every call it tries to make, until a human signs off.\nL181: # call.task_id, call.tool, call.args\nL201: # -- table tools -----------------------------------------------------\nL218: # Retired (legacy_*/deprecated) tables may be dropped as routine\nL219: # maintenance; anything else needs a human to sign off.\nL222: # Access changes always need a human, and are never made on\nL223: # someone else's tables.\nL227: # -- network tools ----------------------------------------------------\nL240: # A partner we have not onboarded yet: hold for approval.\nL256: # An endpoint we have not onboarded yet: hold for approval.\nL261 (docstring of function _parse_url):\n    Return (parsed, normalized) for a url string, or (None, None).",
